A||N||3||polomeno||Help ! something snapped under my shifter||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||12-26-2000||04:26 PM||||Hey .. when i went to go into first today I heard some kind of "snap" or "ping" noise come from under the shifter and now it wont go into first , 2nd , or reverse anymore.. i was able to turn off car and put into second so i could drive it back  home.. i was thinking it might just be a linkage to the shifter cables or something?? any idea's please??<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||12-26-2000||05:01 PM||||something similar happened to me and it ended up being one of my shift cables broke. maybe you could luck out (if you could call it that) and it was just a pin broke and the cable slipped off the shift linkage or it's disconnected at the tranny (probaly not if you say you heard it under the shifter). pretty easy fix once you get the interior pieces off and you can see whats what.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||12-26-2000||05:13 PM||||yes i hope it is something like just a pin.. how difficult was it to change the shifter cable when yours broke??||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||12-26-2000||07:46 PM||||pretty easy, but a lot of my interiors gone so when it happened i pretty much just took my shifter boot and surround off to see the problem. when i got the cable i needed (that turned out to be the hardest part) it was pretty much just thread it into the interior of the car (need to take out computer too or at least move it over) and hook it back up. the interior is really the hard part if it ends up being the cable.  ||||reg||1
